 ### Polyhedral Voxel Construction
-A method to construct voxel landscapes by defining 3D polyhedral shapes and determining which grid points fall within those volumes using point-in-polyhedron algorithms [S5, unofficial]. For every point in the local region of the world grid, apply a 3D point-in-polyhedron method (most often point-in-convex-hull). If a point falls within the volume, set that grid cell as 'present' (a voxel). Repeat for additional shapes to form the terrain [S5, unofficial].
