 ## Background
-Originating from procedural generation techniques in voxel-based games, this method was implemented in web-based WebGL environments [S2, unofficial] and Godot engine C++ extensions [S3, unofficial] around 2025-2026. It builds on the concept of chunked terrain management to handle infinite or large worlds efficiently. The use of octaved noise for height and separate noise for moisture/wackiness allows for diverse biome generation. The technique is used in real-time procedural terrain loading plugins [S2, unofficial].
